"""Tofu Async Server — Quart + Hypercorn (HTTP/2 capable).

This is a drop-in alternative to server.py that uses the Quart async
framework (Pallets project, same team as Flask) with Hypercorn as the
ASGI server. All existing Flask-style sync route handlers run unchanged
in a thread pool.

Usage:
    python server_async.py                    # HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 (h2c)
    python server_async.py --certfile ...     # HTTP/2 with TLS

Benefits over server.py (Werkzeug dev server):
    - HTTP/2 multiplexing (eliminates the 6-connections-per-host limit)
    - True async I/O for any routes converted to async def
    - Production-quality ASGI server (Hypercorn)
    - Sync Flask routes still work (run in thread pool automatically)

The original server.py remains as a stable fallback.
"""

